error[Z0401]: `layout` of `plot` must be a List<Str>, but this is a List<Int>
 --> scripts/main.zeff:6:16
  |
6 | f.plot(layout: [1, 2])
  |                ^^^^^^ a List<Int>
  |
  = help: usage: `g.plot(exposure: Var, outcome: Var, direction: down | right = down, layout: List<Str>, at: Record, same_rank: List<Vars>, spacing: List<Float>)`

error[Z0401]: row 1 of `layout:` has a backtick that is not closed
 --> scripts/main.zeff:6:16
  |
6 | f.plot(layout: ["`u x", "m y"])
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this row
  |
  = help: a name that is not a plain one is written in backticks inside the text, as in the graph

error[Z0401]: `layout:` and `at:` both place the nodes
 --> scripts/main.zeff:6:40
  |
6 | f.plot(layout: [". u .", "x m y"], at: {u: [1, 0], x: [0, 1], m: [1, 1], y: [2, 1]})
  |                                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the nodes are placed twice
  |
  = help: give one of the two: `layout:` for a grid written row by row, `at:` for a column and a row to each node

error[Z0401]: `same_rank:` adjusts the automatic layout, and the script places every node itself
 --> scripts/main.zeff:6:47
  |
6 | f.plot(layout: [". u .", "x m y"], same_rank: [[x, y]])
  |                                               ^^^^^^^^ changes nothing here
  |
  = help: put the nodes on one row of `layout:`, or give them one row in `at:`, and leave `same_rank:` out

error[Z0401]: `same_rank:` asks for `x` and `m` on one layer, and an arrow, or a chain of arrows, leads from one to the other
 --> scripts/main.zeff:6:19
  |
6 | f.plot(same_rank: [[x, m]])
  |                   ^^^^^^^^ cannot share a layer
  |
  = help: a cause stands on a layer before its effect; keep on one layer only nodes that no chain of arrows joins

error[Z0401]: `same_rank:` asks for `x` and `y` on one layer, and an arrow, or a chain of arrows, leads from one to the other
 --> scripts/main.zeff:6:19
  |
6 | f.plot(same_rank: [[x, y]])
  |                   ^^^^^^^^ cannot share a layer
  |
  = help: a cause stands on a layer before its effect; keep on one layer only nodes that no chain of arrows joins

